sts and  attaches their severed heads to a boat  which he sends floating toward category  ragnar uses this very tactic while  trying to terrify the mercians over in  england and it works very well still  kora knows the people of catagette are a  tough breed so for good measure he  crucifies the head priest nailing her to  the mast of the ship  when we return to catagets and vikings  valhalla it's being ruled by yarl hokan  a pagan viking of african descent she  reveals to freitas eric's daughter that  she had dreams in which the water next  to category recedes into the ocean  revealing a bounty of fish the people  believe it to be a blessing from the  gods but when the water returns it  causes widespread death and destruction  of course it's the tsunami that hokan  has dreamed of and one that was  foreshadowed long ago in season 4 of  vikings the opening credits sequence of  vikings has always used the song if i  had a heart by the swedish  singer-songwriter fever-ray though the  imagery was tweaked and updated from  season to season in season four's  opening credits a brief shot shows the  tsunami wiping out cataget but it  doesn't come from the sea it comes from  the direction of the valley how can a  tsunami come from inland as vikings  valhalla season 1 nears its end koran  olaf launched their assault on katagat  they trick koken and her allies into  thinking they will use the high tide  provided by the wolf moon to attack from  the sea when in fact they plan to come  from the other side throwing a wave of  christian warriors at the city  while planning his attack olaf remarks  the walls of cardigan have not been  breached in over 100 years it's a  throwaway comment about a bygone era to  many of his men but those who watched  vikings will know exactly what he's  talking about the category civil war was  one of the major events in the first  series fought between the sons of ragnar  lagertha decides to pounce when they are  away from cataget overthrowing queen  